        <p>
<bold>Mastication Muscles</bold>
</p>
        <p>Chin and malar implants are positioned in regions where the muscles of mastication attach to or closely interact with facial bones. These muscles are critical for mastication and speech and contribute to certain facial expressions. The anterior trunk of CN V3 provides motor innervation. Improper implant placement can cause discomfort and compromise the functional integrity of these muscles. Table 2 summarizes key anatomical and functional information regarding the muscles of mastication.</p>
        <table-wrap id="article-156219.table1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
